// Title: Potentially Suspicious JWT Token Search Via CLI
// ID: 6d3a3952-6530-44a3-8554-cf17c116c615
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), kagebunsher
// Date: 2022-10-25
// Tags: attack.credential-access, attack.t1528, attack.t1552.001
// Description: Detects potentially suspicious search for JWT tokens via CLI by looking for the string "eyJ0eX" or "eyJhbG".
// JWT tokens are often used for access-tokens across various applications and services like Microsoft 365, Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, and others.
// Threat actors may search for these tokens to steal them for lateral movement or privilege escalation.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "eyJ0eXAiOi" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "eyJhbGciOi" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS " eyJ0eX" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS " \"eyJ0eX\"" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS " 'eyJ0eX'" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS " eyJhbG" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS " \"eyJhbG\"" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS " 'eyJhbG'")) AND ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "find " OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "find.exe" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "findstr" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "select-string " OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS "strings")))
